{"time_unix": 1792773405.4586697, "event": "candidate_created", "payload": {"id": "xs-desc-lifetime-v1", "parent": "b2beda7fe460f911b88d27890993347588d70748", "worktree": "worktrees/xswap-p123-2026-10-23/xs-desc-lifetime-v1", "status": "active", "hypothesis": "Descriptor-lifetime fix. Mechanism: shrink publishes the lowered nr_clusters_mapped before synchronize_rcu and drains each removed cluster lock before unmapping; every lookup that may hold a stale entry (swap cache RCU readers, swp_swapcount, swap_entry_swapped, swap_retry_table_alloc, __swap_cache_alloc around its sleeping allocation) goes through an RCU-bounded checked lookup and treats an unmapped cluster as a freed slot. Expected: no descriptor access after unmap; no measurable swap-in latency change. Falsifier: KASAN/lockdep report or data mismatch under a shrink-vs-writeback stress, or >5% swap-in latency regression vs b2beda7f.", "created_unix": 1792773405.4579568, "protocol_sha256": "cbc54c6053eddc9af08bab8db38a251985f6bd71dc3a7f756d692810f91bf93a"}}
